# Copy to .env and edit. Every setting is optional.

# Data providers in priority order, comma-separated: yahoo, finnhub, public, mock
# (plus any provider ids that PLUGINS add).
# For each security the first provider that covers its market sector is used,
# falling back to the next on error.
#   coinbase No key. Real-time crypto prices and trades (XBTUSD, XETUSD, XSOUSD)
#           from Coinbase's public market data; other securities go to the next provider.
#   yahoo   No key. Unofficial Yahoo Finance access; Yahoo's terms prohibit
#           redistribution, so use it for your own personal instance only.
#   finnhub Free key from https://finnhub.io. Free tier covers mainly US
#           equities, with real-time trade streaming. Check Finnhub's terms
#           before sharing data with others.
#   public  No key. US Treasury yield curve, New York Fed rates, World Bank
#           statistics (government / open data), and index members from
#           Wikipedia. Powers GC, BTMM, WB, ECST, MEMB.
#   mock    Simulated prices and research data for development, demos, and offline use.
PROVIDERS=coinbase,yahoo,public

# Required to enable the finnhub provider (it is skipped with a warning otherwise).
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Optional: free key from https://fred.stlouisfed.org to enable the ECO economic calendar.
FRED_API_KEY=

# Server port when running from source. With Docker Compose, use HOST_PORT instead.
# If you change it for `npm run dev`, also start the client with API_URL=http://localhost:<port>.
PORT=8787
# HOST_PORT=8787

# SQLite file for cached price history. Default: data/cache.db in the repo.
# Use :memory: to keep the cache in memory only.
# CACHE_DB=data/cache.db

# How often (ms, minimum 500) streamed quotes are refreshed from polling providers.
# Also how often price alerts (ALRT) are checked.
STREAM_INTERVAL_MS=5000

# --- AI analyst (ASK, and "? question" on any command line) ---------------------
# Leave AI_PROVIDER empty to turn the analyst off.
#   openai     OpenAI or any OpenAI-compatible API (Groq, Together, OpenRouter,
#              vLLM, LM Studio...). Needs AI_API_KEY and AI_MODEL; set AI_BASE_URL
#              for non-OpenAI endpoints, e.g. https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   anthropic  Anthropic Messages API. Needs AI_API_KEY and AI_MODEL.
#   ollama     Local models via Ollama, free and private. Needs AI_MODEL (a model
#              with tool calling, e.g. llama3.1); AI_BASE_URL defaults to
#              http://localhost:11434/v1
#   mock       Scripted answers for demos and tests.
AI_PROVIDER=
AI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL=
# AI_BASE_URL=
# Optional: a stronger model from the same provider for deep research (?? question),
# which plans multi-step analyses. Defaults to AI_MODEL.
# AI_MODEL_DEEP=

# --- Sign-in ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave AUTH unset for a personal terminal. AUTH=password requires accounts, so
# portfolios, sheets, alerts and paper accounts are private to each person.
# AUTH=password
# AUTH_SIGNUP=closed   (stop new accounts once yours exist)

# Name and email for the User-Agent that public APIs (Wikipedia, SEC) ask for.
# Defaults to SEC_USER_AGENT.
# CONTACT=Your Name you@example.com

# --- Plugins (see PLUGINS.md) ----------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated plugin paths (from the repo root) or package names.
# ./plugins/edgar adds CF <GO> (SEC company filings) for US-listed equities.
# PLUGINS=./plugins/edgar
# The SEC requires a User-Agent naming you and a contact email.
# SEC_USER_AGENT=Your Name you@example.com
